17592186349861 1145 "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2}+1,\\,{v}^{3}+1,\\,2u+v⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}+1),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{3}+1),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u+v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,0,\\,2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{3}+1),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u+v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,3{v}^{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2u & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3{v}^{2} & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 3{v}^{2} & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2u & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6{v}^{2},\\,-2u,\\,6u{v}^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535451 true] [17592186349862 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349863 13194139535451 true] [17592186349862 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349864 13194139535451 true] [17592186349862 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349865 13194139535451 true] [17592186349862 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349866 13194139535451 true] [17592186349862 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349867 13194139535451 true] [17592186349862 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535451 true] [17592186349862 1041 "selection" 13194139535451 true] [17592186349862 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349864 13194139535451 true] [17592186349862 1110 #uuid "84d27442-6a52-560d-acea-fb1101a6008e" 13194139535451 true] [17592186349863 1034 "⟨-6{v}^{2}+u,\\,-2u+v,\\,6u{v}^{2}⟩" 13194139535451 true] [17592186349863 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535451 true] [17592186349863 1111 #uuid "2fc04779-ea73-5a07-9c2f-4747f1d4c4e9" 13194139535451 true] [1